#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172649 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172041 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75710e99-e13c-54ba-9401-486bfec15284" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rectangular Regions Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0034a4c6-10b3-508b-8a76-afcee44b5628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360829} {:answer/id #uuid "54b4ecb4-3c90-5cbd-8513-4c588703ab5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361213} {:answer/id #uuid "58ca3b2a-6a23-5aa0-8f8c-eb75ceef12c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361240} {:answer/id #uuid "8c45f8d5-3f54-55ab-8e59-4b349667c905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361455} {:answer/id #uuid "c814eaaa-dc5e-5c70-a113-f897b76f031d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0034a4c6-10b3-508b-8a76-afcee44b5628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360829} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cb2fb3c-0491-59a7-9d61-fd56136a2903" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e86fafab-049b-51e4-93da-aada8761c377" :question/math-academy-id "q-97538" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(x+1)^{2}(y-2)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<-1$ and $y>2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<-1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>-1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(x+1)^{2}(y-2).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=-1$ or $y=2.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/1f/1f4b1b2ca736fb83eff0a4b85a3f479bf99b3b337492d0a77abe739038ed141f.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/fd/fdafadd1631a75c2998aaed5c6bad62a3ea1dcc0ac57d245a00d167e74aa3bb4.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $x<-1$ and $y>2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $x<-1$ and $y<2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $x>-1$ and $y<2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176047 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f349e4de-9f9e-5e92-9b81-db52ad4ba2fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174829} {:answer/id #uuid "0a68b6d8-5320-59e1-af7b-97987406a8dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174830} {:answer/id #uuid "0a8dae36-2ef6-5605-a493-657582045b8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174831} {:answer/id #uuid "2d98a1ad-215c-5402-be54-ee893673f7e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174832} {:answer/id #uuid "539d3879-ca1d-5553-a2b6-dec799b9e7c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174833}] :answer-field/id #uuid "27db85be-39d8-55f8-966f-ff3e095cc9ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174828}] :question/id #uuid "3291f5a6-141c-577f-9e01-4f06e16f89ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-27015" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n1. The function has maximum values at $x = \\frac{π}{2} + nπ$.\n2. The function is zero at $x = \\frac{3π}{2}$.\n3. The range of the function is $[- π, π]$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176047 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cd92769-ca0a-56e4-a143-8bf29d335b41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174835} {:answer/id #uuid "18288890-1a37-5a5f-8cf7-6d8a409b142c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174836} {:answer/id #uuid "28226114-2e37-5a12-9208-11e6e4343147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174837} {:answer/id #uuid "4b1e17e2-a2fe-5af9-94a2-2e198a99d6ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174838} {:answer/id #uuid "77fefe57-810f-5db3-8e76-06d7c2de4ac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174839}] :answer-field/id #uuid "09c7beaa-f9fa-5209-96bf-7daa682b65ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174834}] :question/id #uuid "4431905d-f46d-548a-987b-b6164fd2cc5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-27021" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n1. The zeros of the function are $x = \\frac{π}{2} + nπ$.\n2. The function has maximum values at $x = \\frac{3π}{2} + 2nπ$.\n3. The range of $y = \\cos x$ is $[- 1, 0]$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dadb8ed-d007-53f9-b484-29cf8f9a60a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290758} {:answer/id #uuid "66c9cd18-91c7-5e08-b042-2a46c28131c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291069} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad75161-3e9a-5223-a9dd-e94c64654137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291218} {:answer/id #uuid "8dc52d0d-4f4a-5cc2-b0ef-5fca8c28e540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291239} {:answer/id #uuid "f8178445-42e3-5a5f-bf77-90e72387e35e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dadb8ed-d007-53f9-b484-29cf8f9a60a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290758} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8e4e113-a95b-5d5a-b2fa-1d2198192c93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ac898e3a-bbc1-536e-8415-2d3fbc798e28" :question/math-academy-id "q-27638" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi .$\n- The function returns only positive values on the intervals $(\\pi n,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n)\\,.$\n- The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/32/326418398ce1a33f03a21f3bdb58107856f4ccb72241429f1604486281e60822.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function returns only positive values on the interval $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the function is positive on $(n\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi )\\,.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f15d390-a048-5eb4-a046-310acd367f7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174859} {:answer/id #uuid "e88f93a9-f633-5861-9b67-f9258797c25b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174860} {:answer/id #uuid "448fad8e-383b-5721-928b-2f98064401f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174861} {:answer/id #uuid "47ec71cf-a994-50c7-8ca5-ac57ea5d0ea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174862} {:answer/id #uuid "5ea9d9e5-e787-5660-bc70-c91a945b6f45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174863}] :answer-field/id #uuid "02d7e3e2-9588-558a-8337-8446e8238d6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174858}] :question/id #uuid "95d49fd8-cd30-53eb-a4a3-b8a8c0494e55" :question/math-academy-id "q-27660" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\tan x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n1. The function has asymptotes at $x = \\frac{π}{2} + πn$.\n2. The range of the function is $y ∈ (-\\frac{π}{2}, \\frac{π}{2})$.\n3. The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x = nπ$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176487 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4d9a5b4-143b-5f70-96af-c54653decc87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175061} {:answer/id #uuid "bc66d19e-5e0e-5472-94a8-e7027abf7aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175062} {:answer/id #uuid "d19b760d-4b8d-5e73-9344-5302538b3f30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175063} {:answer/id #uuid "d982c693-68ac-55c9-a06f-bf9fdb410dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175064} {:answer/id #uuid "0d82be89-281b-59c1-8ba2-fc6631fb56f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175065}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f4ea36c4-9c29-57d9-8e19-0b623c6933dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175060}] :question/id #uuid "5961bc49-07f6-5191-b949-28358553d498" :question/math-academy-id "q-42912" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\csc x$? Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\n1. The point $(π,-1)$ is not on the graph.\n2. The function has a vertical asymptotes at $x = nπ$.\n3. The value $y = 2$ is in the range of the function."}] [{:db/id #edb/re